/ A test's tags are its goal's own, stamped when it is built: two tag steps give it the union of theirs. The test
/ reads its own tags as the runner does, by discovering itself.
TestTagAccumulatesUserTagsOnRun
- tag this test 'http'
- tag this test 'fast', 'slow'
- test.discover tests in '.', pattern='TestTagAccumulatesUserTagsOnRun.test.goal', write to %tests%
- get first item from %tests%, write to %me%
- list.contains %me.tags% has 'http', write to %hasHttp%
- assert %hasHttp% is true
- list.contains %me.tags% has 'fast', write to %hasFast%
- assert %hasFast% is true
- list.contains %me.tags% has 'slow', write to %hasSlow%
- assert %hasSlow% is true
